faqs:
  - q: "Who can see a member’s records?"
    a: "The member, and the society’s staff who work with their branch. Some details are only for staff, like who recorded a payment. These aren’t shown in the member’s app. Members never see disciplinary records."
  - q: "Where is our data kept?"
    a: "In secure online databases and private file storage. Everything is encrypted (scrambled so others can’t read it), both when it is sent and when it is stored. Files such as receipts and documents are private. Only people who are allowed can open them."
  - q: "Can we take our data with us?"
    a: "Yes, on every plan. Your leaders can download all of your society’s data. Each member can download their own."
  - q: "What happens to our data if we close our society on CoopCircle?"
    a: "Your president can close the society for a while, or for good. Before anything is deleted, your leaders are told, and they can download everything."
  - q: "How do I report a security problem?"
    a: "Please contact us straight away through the contact page. We will deal with it first."
